   ],
   "spoken": "With the knight already on c6 and the pawn to d6, Black steers into an offbeat Nimzowitsch/Philidor-flavoured setup. White simply builds the centre with d4 and enjoys more space.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "Against the Nimzowitsch Defense, occupy the centre — the offbeat move order concedes space.",
   "plans": "Build the big centre and develop."
